WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.120
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:08.020
Валком-то привет, русский эписот 44, 49 июня, 2026 года.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.160
I am all-in-regat-sem-great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:13.940
Поехали, let's go!

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:16.380
Today our theme is animals.

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:20.160
So our word of the day is животное.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.720
Да ты с животное Е.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:24.880
Сэйт слол и витми.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.820
Живот на Е.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.980
На отначеру спит животное.

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:32.700
Это минс-анимал.

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:37.420
Имачен охол зу-фулов животное Е Фрэнс.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:39.480
Хереза Симпл Сэйнтенс.

00:00:40.040 --> 00:00:41.460
Это большое животное.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.680
Это минс, this is a big animal.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.580
Now repeat after me.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.260
Живот на Е.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:52.400
We already know Sloan from before.

00:00:53.040 --> 00:00:57.480
That means elephant and size, which means hair.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.840
Now let's add more animal words.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.520
The first one is птица.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:06.720
Птица repeat after me.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:07.600
Птица.

00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:09.800
Птица means bored.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:14.640
The example sentence is птица летает в небе.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:17.720
That translates as the bird flies in the sky.

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:22.120
The memory hook notes that pits a sound like twitsa.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.280
This hook fits a singing board perfectly.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.280
Next is рыба.

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:29.940
Оройба repeat after me.

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:32.940
Оройба, рыба means fish.

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.760
The example sentence is рыба плавает воде.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:40.320
That translates as the fish swims in the water.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:44.760
The memory hook says array, b, rhyme sweet, рыба.

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:47.940
This image fits a fish during the backstroke.

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:50.020
Now we have кит.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:50.700
Кит.

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:51.800
Repeat after me.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:01:52.440
Кит.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:53.920
Кит means whale.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:57.460
The example sentence is кит очень большой.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.900
That translates as the whale is very big.

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:05.500
The memory hook notes that кит sounds like eat.

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:10.340
This hook fits a well that eats tons of tiny fish.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.420
Next comes утка.

00:02:13.060 --> 00:02:15.340
О, утка repeat after me.

00:02:15.840 --> 00:02:18.340
О, утка, утка means duck.

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:22.360
The example sentence is утка плавает на озере.

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:26.240
That translates as the duck swims on the lake.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:31.740
The memory hook says, о утика sounds like ут as an hood.

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.420
This hook fits a duck that quacks instead.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.740
На лорич медведь.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:40.360
Медведет repeat after me.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:41.280
Медведет.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:43.500
Медведь means bear.

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:47.520
The example sentence is медведь любит мед.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:51.220
That translates as the bear loves honey.

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.000
The memory hook states that

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.700
medvaida literally means honey noir.

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.260
This hook fits a bear who knows where the honey is.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:03.000
Then черепаха.

00:03:03.420 --> 00:03:05.480
Черепаха repeat after me.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:08.720
Черепаха черепаха means turtle.

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.880
The example sentence is черепаха медленно ползёт.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:17.220
That translates as the turtle crawls slowly.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:23.360
The memory hook notes that черепаха haspa like papa.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.540
This image fits a slow grandpa turtle.

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:28.700
Next is бабочка.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.940
Бея бабочка repeat after me.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:35.340
Бея бабочка бабочка means butterfly.

00:03:36.180 --> 00:03:39.980
The example sentence is бабочка красивая.

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:43.500
That translates as the butterfly is beautiful.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.880
The memory hook says, бея бабочка.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.420
Sounds like бабочка.

00:03:49.060 --> 00:03:51.640
This hook fits a fancy flying bow tie.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:54.320
Ласт из ящерится.

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:58.660
Я щи рица, репит авторми.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:04.080
Я щи рица, я щи рица means lizard.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:08.700
The example sentence is я щи рица бегает быстро.

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:12.480
That translates as the lizard runs fast.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:18.020
The memory hook notes that я щи рица has shellac.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.540
This hook fits a lizard that says while hiding.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:25.340
Now for quick grammar bite.

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:27.500
Russian nouns have genders.

00:04:28.040 --> 00:04:31.020
They can be masculine, feminine or neuter.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:33.380
Adjective must match the noun.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:35.100
Look at our animals.

00:04:35.980 --> 00:04:38.360
Большой кит, that is a big whale.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:41.020
The ending changes for masculine.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:44.300
Большая птица, that is a big bird.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:47.040
The ending changes for feminine.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:49.060
Большое животное.

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.080
That is a big animal.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.620
The ending changes for neuter.

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:56.620
It is like a matching game once you see the pattern.

00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.640
Now here is something really cool about one of today's words.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.500
Want to know a secret about медведь?

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.680
The Russian word медведь

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:09.220
and the idea of a honey eater share the same concept.

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:13.880
They both come from the ancient Slavic words for honey and to know.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.300
People were afraid to say the real name of the bear out loud.

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:21.560
This word started in Proto-Slavic.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:24.020
It travelled through all Russian folk tales.

00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:27.360
It stayed in modern Russian as a gentle nickname.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:32.200
The Russian word медведь sounds nothing like the English bear.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.640
Yet both animals love the same sweet treat.

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:38.360
Next time you see honey, remember.

00:05:38.880 --> 00:05:40.760
It is cousin Свет медведь.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:44.100
They both come from the same honey-loving root.

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:48.460
That connection is your secret shortcut to remembering it forever.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.780
In Russian theory tales,

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:54.340
animal often act like wise teachers or tricky friends.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:59.580
Think of the clever fox or the strong bear in stories by Pushkin.

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.460
Kids grow up hearing these tales.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.320
This makes animal words extra fun and memorable.

00:06:07.120 --> 00:06:11.540
Details help when you visit Russia or talk with Russian-speaking family.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:13.500
Now it is practice time.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:15.880
Do you remember what a rib means?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:17.220
It means fish.

00:06:17.780 --> 00:06:22.840
Try this challenge for kids, draw your favorite animal and label it with the Russian word.

00:06:23.720 --> 00:06:26.740
Say, et-op-titsa out loud, why you do it?

00:06:27.180 --> 00:06:33.720
For adults next time you see a pet or zoo animal describe it in Russian using one new word.

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:39.280
Say, et-op-titsa outka, and send the sentence to a friend learning with you.

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:41.640
Молодец, that means well done.

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.980
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:49.240
Practice saying today's words out loud, even just once,

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.160
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:55.740
See you next time, пока, that's Russian for buy.

